> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Lojban+For+Beginners&bl

You'll find Lojban for Beginners (aka. "le velcli be fi la lojban. bei loi co'a
cilre") especially helpful. It's a great tutorial, a little old, not
really up to date,
yet there's only one feature of the logical language that has changed
remarkably: You should know that {lo} has become the generic article
instead of {le}, what is mostly used in the velcli to make "nouns" out of
"assertions".
This new usage is called "xorlo" since xorxes was the one to come up with
this proposal.
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=How+to+use+xorlo

mi'e.darves.


